## Acquisition

How an item came into someone's possession: what was paid, when, where from, and against which reference.

```ts
import { Acquisition } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/collectibles/acquisition';

@field acquisition = contains(Acquisition);
```

`price` is the base `AmountWithCurrency`, so an acquisition carries its own currency. `source` is free text (Retail, a resale platform, a local meetup) because the useful list differs per collector; a consumer that wants a select supplies its own options. `reference` holds whatever proves the purchase: an order number, a receipt id or a lot number. The atom and embedded views format the price through the cluster's money formatter, so 11.50 never renders as 11.5.

### Non-goals

It does not record what an item is worth now; that is a reporting rollup over active listings.
